1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,597
Reports show what happened in your contact center and your C.R.M.

2
00:00:05,597 --> 00:00:07,604
over a period you choose.

3
00:00:07,604 --> 00:00:11,943
This video shows how to find a report, set its date range and

4
00:00:11,943 --> 00:00:15,180
filters, and export it to CSV, Excel or PDF.

5
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:23,636
A report answers a question about work that already happened:

6
00:00:23,636 --> 00:00:29,450
how many calls came in, how many were answered, and which campaign turned leads into customers.

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,298
Every number is worked out from your records when you open the report,

8
00:00:34,298 --> 00:00:36,617
so it always matches what you picked:

9
00:00:36,617 --> 00:00:38,720
the period, the queue, the agent.

10
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:43,330
You read the figures on screen, or take them away as a file

11
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:46,240
for a spreadsheet, a meeting or an archive.

12
00:00:50,473 --> 00:00:54,378
Every report lives under Reports in the admin menu.

13
00:00:54,378 --> 00:00:56,775
They are grouped by category:

14
00:00:56,775 --> 00:01:04,103
Operations, Agent Performance, Queue and Routing, Workforce and Payroll, CRM and Campaigns, and more.

15
00:01:04,617 --> 00:01:07,212
Reports itself opens the Reports page:

16
00:01:07,212 --> 00:01:12,107
one card for each report you may open, with a line that says what it answers.

17
00:01:12,657 --> 00:01:15,874
Click a card, or pick the report from the menu.

18
00:01:15,874 --> 00:01:18,847
Here it is Call insights, under Operations.

19
00:01:23,084 --> 00:01:26,063
Which reports you see depends on your role.

20
00:01:26,063 --> 00:01:29,345
Under Roles, search the permissions for reports.

21
00:01:29,345 --> 00:01:35,181
View Contact Center reports opens the Contact Center reports, and View Omnichannel reports

22
00:01:35,181 --> 00:01:37,674
opens the CRM and campaign reports.

23
00:01:38,203 --> 00:01:44,235
Another report can bring a permission of its own, such as Run Phone Number Verifications Report.

24
00:01:44,235 --> 00:01:47,133
Give a role only the ones its members need.

25
00:01:48,833 --> 00:01:54,385
This is the Reports page of a user whose role has only View Contact Center reports.

26
00:01:54,385 --> 00:02:00,063
The Contact Center reports are listed; the CRM reports, such as Lead funnel, are not.

27
00:02:04,287 --> 00:02:07,295
The top of every report is its filter bar.

28
00:02:07,295 --> 00:02:12,497
The first filter is the Date range, and its button states the range in words.

29
00:02:12,989 --> 00:02:14,556
Click it to choose.

30
00:02:14,556 --> 00:02:17,753
Relative days run from Today to Last 90 Days.

31
00:02:17,753 --> 00:02:22,956
Calendar periods cover this week, this month, this quarter and this year, and

32
00:02:22,956 --> 00:02:24,649
the ones before them.

33
00:02:25,157 --> 00:02:30,007
Rolling months cover the last three, six or twelve months.

34
00:02:30,007 --> 00:02:34,933
Custom Range takes a start and an end, and On or before and

35
00:02:34,933 --> 00:02:37,737
On or after leave one end open.

36
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:40,623
Pick Last 30 Days, and click Show.

37
00:02:40,623 --> 00:02:43,289
The report runs again for that period.

38
00:02:45,256 --> 00:02:48,239
The summary shows the totals as cards:

39
00:02:48,239 --> 00:02:56,103
total calls, inbound and outbound, answered, abandoned, voicemail, callback requests, failures, average handle

40
00:02:56,103 --> 00:02:58,746
time and average speed of answer.

41
00:02:59,222 --> 00:03:03,788
Below, the same calls are broken down by channel, by outcome and by

42
00:03:03,788 --> 00:03:09,042
day, so one page answers the first questions and points to where to look next.

43
00:03:13,225 --> 00:03:17,293
Each report offers the filters that make sense for it.

44
00:03:17,293 --> 00:03:22,445
Call insights offers Queue group, Queue, Agent, Direction and Channel.

45
00:03:22,897 --> 00:03:26,142
A filter left on All does not narrow the report.

46
00:03:26,142 --> 00:03:30,407
Pick the Support queue and the Inbound direction, and click Show.

47
00:03:30,859 --> 00:03:34,783
Every number is worked out again from the matching records:

48
00:03:34,783 --> 00:03:40,579
the cards, the breakdowns and the daily volume now describe only inbound calls to Support.

49
00:03:41,029 --> 00:03:43,749
Other reports have other filters.

50
00:03:43,749 --> 00:03:49,119
Dialer call detail filters by campaign, source, status and disposition.

51
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:54,400
In Disposition you can tick several dispositions at once, to list the numbers

52
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,030
that ended either way.

53
00:04:00,256 --> 00:04:03,599
The Export menu sits above the report.

54
00:04:03,599 --> 00:04:10,588
With the Excel and PDF features on, it offers Export CSV, Export Excel and Export PDF.

55
00:04:10,588 --> 00:04:15,906
With only the Reports feature, it is a single Export CSV button.

56
00:04:16,357 --> 00:04:21,053
An export uses the same date range and filters as the report on

57
00:04:21,053 --> 00:04:26,974
screen, and keeps the detail rows, subtotals and grand totals in the order shown.

58
00:04:26,974 --> 00:04:29,697
Export CSV downloads a plain file.

59
00:04:30,174 --> 00:04:34,684
Export Excel puts each section of the report on its own worksheet.

60
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:42,170
Export PDF lays the report out as it looks on screen, with its

61
00:04:42,170 --> 00:04:44,420
charts, and numbers the pages.

62
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:49,955
This is the start of the CSV file the browser just saved.

63
00:04:49,955 --> 00:04:54,016
Its name holds the report and the first and last day of the

64
00:04:54,016 --> 00:04:56,890
period, and it opens in any spreadsheet.

65
00:04:57,640 --> 00:05:02,009
The Excel workbook has one worksheet for each section of the report:

66
00:05:02,009 --> 00:05:06,260
the summary, and the breakdowns by channel, by outcome and by day.

67
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:10,026
And this is the first page of the PDF:

68
00:05:10,026 --> 00:05:12,700
the report as it looks on screen.

69
00:05:16,883 --> 00:05:21,849
Reports on agents' time read every state change of every agent, so they

70
00:05:21,849 --> 00:05:23,784
cover 31 days at a time.

71
00:05:23,784 --> 00:05:27,783
Pick Last 90 Days on Agent time summary, and click Show.

72
00:05:28,235 --> 00:05:32,857
The report says the period is too long, and names the longest period

73
00:05:32,857 --> 00:05:36,106
it allows, instead of showing partial figures.

74
00:05:36,106 --> 00:05:39,105
Pick Last 30 Days, and the figures return.

75
00:05:40,689 --> 00:05:44,684
A report that measures work from a feature your site does not use

76
00:05:44,684 --> 00:05:48,061
shows a notice naming that feature, instead of zeroes.

77
00:05:48,061 --> 00:05:53,239
Here the Contact Center Call Recording feature is off, and Recording coverage says so.

78
00:05:57,439 --> 00:05:59,266
A weekly service review:

79
00:05:59,266 --> 00:06:03,957
open Queue service level for Last Week, filter by queue group, and read

80
00:06:03,957 --> 00:06:06,029
where calls waited too long.

81
00:06:06,779 --> 00:06:08,919
A figure for someone else:

82
00:06:08,919 --> 00:06:13,401
export Excel for a finance team that wants rows, or PDF for a

83
00:06:13,401 --> 00:06:15,609
manager who wants the page.

84
00:06:16,359 --> 00:06:20,213
Reports can also be emailed on a schedule, shown as tiles on a

85
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:23,841
dashboard, and built from scratch with the Report Builder.

86
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:25,769
Those have their own videos.

87
00:06:27,769 --> 00:06:31,523
Reports turn the history of your contact center and your C.R.M.

88
00:06:31,523 --> 00:06:34,134
into figures you can filter and take away.

89
00:06:34,134 --> 00:06:35,549
Thanks for watching.

